 "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Dhurandar 3 ka plot mat leak karo @⁨Akshay⁩", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:56:50Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Naman: 5, Pavan: 10, Srijan: 10, Sayu: 5, Vats: 10", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:57:06Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Pakistan is the undisputed heavyweight of ice outside the polar regions, housing over 7,200 (recent inventories suggest up to 13,000) glaciers across the Karakoram, Himalayas, and Hindu Kush ranges. This massive frozen reservoir acts as a \"water tower,\" feeding the Indus River and providing nearly 75% of the country's freshwater.", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:57:30Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "I would love to see @⁨Akshay⁩ in the next part 😂", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:57:33Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "the Biafo and Hispar glaciers connect to create a 100km \"ice highway,\" the longest continuous glacial system outside the Arctic and Antarctic. Paradoxically, while most of the world's ice is melting, some glaciers here are actually stable or thickening—a scientific mystery famously called the \"Karakoram Anomaly.\"", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:57:43Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Paani 😂 ‎GIF omitted", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:58:08Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Next q", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:58:42Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "5. Most people know the Berlin Wall. Many know the Great Wall. Almost no one talks about this one. Stretching approximately 1,700 miles across the shifting sands, it is one of the longest military structures on earth. Built in stages through the 1980s, it is not a wall of stone or concrete — it is a berm of sand and rock, reinforced with radar sensors, observation posts, and one of the densest antipersonnel minefields anywhere in the world. It divides a disputed territory between the state controlling its western half and a liberation movement controlling the east. The conflict it represents has never been formally resolved.\nId X (the structure's common name) and Y (the disputed territory it runs through)", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:58:56Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Morocco", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:58:56Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "US-Mexico", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:58:59Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Sahara", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:59:00Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Morocco", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:59:00Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Sahara", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:59:02Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Western", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:59:03Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Western Sahara", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T15:59:03Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Israel-WestBank", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"times